/*
 * sealed-deadline.compact — cutoff is sealed; claim uses blockTimeLt.
 *
 * Official pattern (not an invented API):
 *   https://docs.midnight.network/guides/security-best-practices
 *   "Enforcing a deadline". A sealed ledger field is set once, during
 *   construction. blockTimeLt(time) is true when the current block time
 *   is before time. There is no raw block-time accessor. Block time is
 *   accurate to the scale of blocks, not seconds, and is not a randomness
 *   source. The sample assert message is "expired".
 *
 * Upstream tracking: midnightntwrk/midnight-docs#1387
 * Compact reference pages are copied from LFDT-Minokawa/compact. This file
 * does not edit those pages and does not fix the public indexer or node.
 *
 * Language pin: Compact ~0.31.1 / language ~0.23.
 * LOCAL-TRUE. Source only. Not compiled here. Not deployed.
